url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  A small, standard-library Python program that generates a WorldHoloBridge
  conference plan for one country from a country profile. The ACOA brief is
  the fixed content (six conference phases, five holographic tiers, twelve
  governance rules, the adopted demo tiers, the 90-day Country Node pilot);
  the country profile is the variable content (languages, cultural
  authorities, flagship sectors, venues, funding body, disability
  organizations, consent law). Built-in profiles: Canada, Morocco, Germany,
  France, United Kingdom. A new country is a copied JSON file, no code
  change. Every generated plan is checked by 19 tests for all six phases,
  all five tiers, both worked examples (Hall of Memory museum, Cadre
  artistique publicity), the full twelve-rule governance checklist, and the
  demo tiers at the adopted prices. The companion plan document
  (docs/holographic-phygital-society-plan.md) sets out the framework: one
  conference, two engines; demos by appointment; the code open, the service
  the product; consent first, sponsor firewall, guardrails that cannot be
  disabled. All ideas are sparkainlp-x's own; third-party products
  (Looking Glass, Sony ELF-MN1) and the Marie Curie example figure are
  named as products and examples, not claimed as ideas.
keywords:
